NAME
       man - an interface to the system reference manuals

SYNOPSIS
       man [SECTION] NAME...
       man -k KEYWORD
       man -f NAME
       apropos KEYWORD
       whatis NAME

DESCRIPTION
       Show the manual page for NAME in a pager. Pages are stored in
       /usr/share/man as NAME.SECTION. Sections: 1 user commands, 5 file
       formats, 7 overviews, 8 system administration.

OPTIONS
       -k KEYWORD
           search names and descriptions of all pages (apropos); man -k . lists
           everything

       -f NAME
           print the one-line description of NAME (whatis)

       -w
           print the location of the page instead of showing it

PAGER KEYS
       j, Down, Enter     one line down          k, Up      one line up
       Space, f, PgDn     one page down          b, PgUp    one page up
       d / u              half a page down/up    g / G      beginning / end
       /TEXT              search forward         ?TEXT      search backward
       n / N              next / previous match  h          short help
       q, Esc, Ctrl+C     quit

WRITING PAGES
       A page is plain text. A line that starts at column 0 is a section heading. Indented lines whose
       first word starts with - are options and are highlighted. **text** is bold, __text__ underlined.

EXAMPLES
       man ls
       man 8 reboot
       man -k file
       man man

SEE ALSO
       less(1), help(1), intro(1)
